    "notes": "Hard caps are deliberate. Reject VFX-oriented scan/geometry-node assets rather than normalizing multi-million-triangle sources into the game pipeline. Source package size is measured for the exact requested glTF resolution plus dependencies before download."
  },
  "notes": "Source species are visual/ecological analogues for Asterra, not literal Earth taxonomy. Surface textures are intentionally deferred to a later terrain-material milestone. Heavy VFX assets above the selection policy are excluded even when they look excellent.",
  "biome_plan": {
    "OCEAN": "No generic v1 mesh scatter. Deep ocean waits for a verified CC0 benthic/kelp/coral set; bathymetric rock remains terrain/geology.",
    "SHELF_SEA": "Sparse coastal stones, ledges and pebble patches. Dedicated kelp/seagrass remains an explicit asset gap.",
    "ICE_CAP": "Extremely sparse exposed stone and boulder scatter only where ice/snow cover permits.",
    "TUNDRA": "Low moss, short/dry grass, low weeds, small shrubs, stones and occasional boulders; no tall canopy.",
    "TAIGA": "Lightweight fir/pine forms, moss, fern, low shrubs, mossy rocks, roots, stumps and fallen logs. Mature conifer diversity remains a future lightweight-asset gap rather than using 8-17M triangle VFX trees.",
    "COLD_DESERT": "Sparse dry grass, quartz/stone scatter, weathered boulders and dead plant debris.",
    "TEMPERATE_GRASSLAND": "Dense varied grass presentation from lightweight grass plus scale/tint clustering, weeds, small flowers, sparse shrubs, stones and rare boulders.",
    "TEMPERATE_FOREST": "Lightweight broadleaf canopy analogues, shrubs, fern/moss, roots, stumps, fallen logs and mossy rocks.",
    "TEMPERATE_RAINFOREST": "Dense moss/fern/shrub layer, lightweight broadleaf canopy analogues, deadwood, exposed roots and moss-covered rocks.",
    "MEDITERRANEAN": "Dry grass, dense scrub, dry branches, stones and warm weathered boulders; avoid the former multi-million-triangle coastal-tree scans.",
    "STEPPE": "Patchy dry grasses, low shrubs, weeds, stones and occasional boulders/dead debris.",
    "HOT_DESERT": "Succulents and desert shrubs at low density, dry leaves/branches, quartz stones and weathered desert boulders.",
    "SAVANNA": "Grass matrix, scattered shrubs, lightweight broadleaf/desert trees, deadwood and exposed rocks.",
    "TROPICAL_SEASONAL_FOREST": "Lightweight broadleaf canopy, tropical shrubs/groundcover, seasonal grass openings, deadwood and roots.",
    "TROPICAL_RAINFOREST": "Dense lightweight broadleaf canopy/understory, fern, moss, shrubs, roots, deadwood and mossy rocks.",
    "WETLAND": "Wet grasses, fern, nettle/weed groundcover, shrubs and sparse moisture-tolerant lightweight trees. Reeds/cattails remain a v1 asset gap.",
    "ALPINE": "Sparse low grass/moss in sheltered areas with dominant stones, scree and boulders; no trees above treeline.",
    "BARE_ROCK": "Geology-driven stones, boulders and ledges; only rare crevice moss/grass when climate allows."
  },
